--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
WHAT SHIPPED (full parity, no stubs)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
A production-polished, native Apple-idiomatic AutomationPresetGallery at parity with the
web source — a responsive card grid of automation preset templates. Decomposed per the
established surface convention:

  PresetGallery.Adapter.swift   pure core (Foundation-only): PresetGallerySurface slug,
                                AutomationTriggerKind (+ web triggerLabels), the iconMap
                                (Lucide -> SF Symbols, web `?? Shield` default),
                                AutomationPresetItem, phase/status/connection enums,
                                AutomationPresetGalleryProjection (resolvePhase,
                                triggerLabel, "{{count}} actions", "Install {{name}}",
                                symbolName), AutomationPresetGalleryAccessibility.
  PresetGallery.Seams.swift     P1/S11 telemetry (view.opened), P1/S10 strings facade,
                                P1 navigator seam (web useNavigate ->
                                /automations/new?preset={id}), the P1/S8 source protocol +
                                update snapshot + in-memory source. No view HTTP.
  PresetGallery.Model.swift     @MainActor @Observable state holder; start/stop/refresh,
                                install(_:), apply(update), stale->one auto-refresh,
                                offline keeps cached items; .text Text helper.
  PresetGallery.States.swift    loading (web four PresetCardSkeleton in the grid), empty
                                (TSEmptyState + clock glyph), error + Retry, inline error,
                                freshness chip (Live/Stale/Offline), connectivity banner.
  PresetGallery.Views.swift     adaptive LazyVGrid (web grid-cols-1/2/3/4), staggered
                                cards, AutomationPresetCard (TSGlassPanel + TSIconBox +
                                name + trigger subtitle + TSBadge action-count + summary +
                                TSButton Install).
  PresetGallery.swift           the View: TSFadeIn, connectivity banner when not live,
                                phase switch (loading/error/empty/content), surfaceSlug.
  PresetGallery.Previews.swift  one #Preview per state (content/empty/loading/error/
                                stale/offline).
  PresetGallery.strings         P1/S10 catalog (table "PresetGallery"): every web key
                                (automations.builder.trigger{Schedule,Event,Geofence,
                                Signal}, automations.builder.noTrigger,
                                automations.presets.{actionCount,install,empty}) + envelope
                                keys (title/loading/errors.load/retry/live/stale/offline/
                                staleBanner/offlineBanner/installAria).
  PresetGallery.Tests.swift     projection + trigger + interpolation + icon + a11y units.
  PresetGallery.ModelTests.swift state-holder units (view.opened once/idempotent, phase
                                transitions, install-seam, stale auto-refresh, offline).

Shared-component mapping (web -> native): GlassPanel->TSGlassPanel, Button->TSButton,
Badge->TSBadge, IconBox->TSIconBox, EmptyState->TSEmptyState, Skeleton->TSSkeleton,
FadeIn->TSFadeIn, StaggerContainer/Item->TSStaggerContainer/Item. Tokens (P1/S9):
Color.TS / Font.TS / TSSpacing / TSRadius. Telemetry slug = "PresetGallery" (P1/S11).
Accessibility: VoiceOver labels on the gallery + every card + the Install button; Dynamic
Type via tokens; reduce-motion honored by TSFadeIn/TSStaggerItem.

NAMING NOTE (collision fix): the predecessor surface AlertMessageEditor already declares
module-scope PresetGalleryPhase/Projection/EmptyState/ErrorState/LoadingState (its own
alert-preset gallery). Editing AlertMessageEditor.* is forbidden (covenant #7), so THIS
surface's Swift types are namespaced AutomationPresetGallery* / AutomationPresetCard* to
avoid the clash. The diagnostics slug and the i18n table name remain the verbatim
"PresetGallery"; the files remain PresetGallery.* per the prompt's allowed-files list.

